   "check": "05-area",
   "result": "content/results/check-05-area.json",
   "sha256": "0f780ffd0c709147211685170d38e8d3d1100de642d9688918a79d75b3616a55",
   "external": [
    "pyproj 3.8.0 / GeographicLib geodesic areas",
    "an independent closed-form spherical area"
   ],
   "criterion": "relative difference at most 1e-9 against an independent expression of the declared spherical formula, over five boundaries including one with a hole",
   "outcome": "agrees",
   "measured": "Implementation: relative difference at most 4.78e-14. Reported separately as method context, not as failures — against a geodesic area with great-circle edges on the same sphere, boxes differ by under 0.01 % and a mid-latitude triangle with oblique edges by 0.30 %; against WGS84 the declared spherical approximation runs +0.45 % at the equator to -0.56 % at 60 N, so its sign changes with latitude.",
   "ranAt": "2026-10-08T23:00:00Z",
   "note": "Three questions kept apart: whether the widget computes the formula it declares, how far that formula is from a great-circle-edged geodesic area, and how far from an ellipsoidal one. Only the first is a criterion; the other two quantify the approximation the widget already discloses when it calls its result approximate."
  },
