   "note": "Compared against the implementation the original case study used: Advanced-1 NB03 reaches its isochrones with nx.ego_graph. The 5 mm residual is exactly the half-step of the two decimal places Fieldwork publishes, so the only disagreement is its rounding. Both traversals run on the edge lengths the fixture states and neither measures a street, so a wrong network passes in both. Covers outbound travel from one origin on one network; inbound is unexercised. Re-run against 0.3.0 after that release added speedMPerMin and travelMode to each junction: the parity validator refused evidence covering 0.2.0 while 0.3.0 was current, and the change being additive was not grounds for carrying the old result forward."
