   "note": "The corridor is rebuilt from the widget's stated rule with GEOS, not compared feature by feature, so the selection arithmetic is reproduced independently. The 0.116% residual is two engines approximating a 25 m radius at 8 segments per quadrant in two different projections, and the symmetric difference being the same size says it is spread around the boundary rather than a missing piece. Covers the five minute band of one corridor, outbound. Both implementations trust the same street lengths and geometry, so a wrong network passes in both. The notebook beside it measures the corridor's area at 0.51x for a 10 m half-width and 1.53x at 60 m, against a 25 m figure the case study records no reason for."
